# Build outputs of the figure pipeline, deliberately not tracked.
#
# The repository tracks the code that generates the article's figures; the
# figures themselves are produced by running it (see README.md, "Rebuilding
# everything from a clean clone").  Commiting 24 MB of carriers that any reader
# can regenerate byte-for-byte would only make the clone heavy, and it would
# let a carrier drift away from its script without anything noticing.
#
# To ship a carrier into version control on purpose, force it:
#     git add -f figures/PhyloRecViewer-手稿正文-图1.pdf
#
# Carriers written next to the scripts by `phylorec_style.save()` and `export.sh`
# (and by PR_FIG_OUT).
*.svg
*.png
*.pdf
*.tif
*.tiff

# Generated inputs and generated reports.  The repository root's .gitignore
# already covers any directory named `_build`; this restates it locally so the
# rule is visible where the files are produced.
_build/
__pycache__/
